 r"I am writing to apply for the Data Scientist position at Perspectum. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have built and validated machine learning models on biomedical data and evaluated AI systems against clinical standards. I am particularly interested in this role because it combines applied machine learning with the rigour of algorithmic validation in a clinical product.",

 r"What attracts me most to Perspectum is that its algorithms sit inside products used in clinical care and clinical trials, so model performance has to be demonstrated, documented and trusted rather than simply reported. I enjoy taking an unclear clinical or business problem and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved, and I am motivated by research that ends up changing how patients are assessed.",

 r"My MSc dissertation used 458,840 UK Biobank participants to build cardiovascular risk prediction models, comparing logistic regression with three tree ensembles. I paid as much attention to calibration as to discrimination, and the final models reached AUCs of 0.714 to 0.718 with near-perfect calibration. I then used doubly robust causal forests on 71,428 participants to estimate the effects of lifestyle change, ran sensitivity analyses for timing, overlap and unmeasured confounding, and validated externally in a separate cohort. The results are delivered in an interactive Streamlit application. This work taught me that a model is only as useful as the evidence that it behaves as expected on data it has not seen.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a patient-facing medical AI engagement for a pharmaceutical client. I designed a 246-question benchmark and six-dimension rubric with the client's clinical experts, which the client adopted as its acceptance standard, built the Python pipeline that scored more than 2,400 responses from six LLMs, and designed blinded paired A/B tests of a medically reviewed knowledge graph. At UCL I also led a group project that fine-tuned ClinicalBERT and PubMedBERT-style models on radiology reports, compared them against simpler baselines, and examined where vision-language models failed against signals derived from the reports.",

 r"Before my MSc I worked as a Research Data Analyst at Westlake University on multi-omics data from ageing skin stem cells, where I refactored and parallelised the processing pipeline in Python and R and cut processing time by around 60 per cent. My Imperial final-year project built a Python pipeline over hundreds of gigabytes of molecular dynamics simulation output. At TikTok Shop UK I analyse operations data in SQL and Python and built an AI agent with Claude Code that automates parts of my team's analytics workflow.",

